#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD1011 expect=skipped domain=ADLBC
#note "PARAMN is listed in the rule's _wildcardExclude, so WildcardExpander drops it as a seed; with no other column ending in N or C there is no capture tuple at all, the expander returns NoMatch and the rule DOES NOT EXECUTE. That is skipped, never noViolation - `no matching column` is an execution-state fact, and noViolation would assert execution. The row deliberately carries a populated PARAMN with an empty PARAM, i.e. data that would fire were PARAMN not excluded, which is what makes this the pin that _wildcardExclude is doing real work."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAM   type=Char
col PARAMN  type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 |  | 1
